drawWalkT -- step 2 toward the first PDF (Tony, 2026-11-07): the draw walk, in kant (utilities' drawWalk). It walks a
form parent before child, depth first, and fills each field that names a fill; a field with no fill is skipped, not
refused. The display is opened by makeDisplay before the walk, as step 1 built it.

Rows (genLadder/pop.sh): DW-1 to DW-4 are one pixel per depth: the top's wall where heading has no fill, words at
depth 1, space (no fill) and ok at depth 2. DW-4 is the depth row: a walk that stops at the top reads wall there. The
refusal count between the walk markers is 0, paired with DW-2 and DW-4, which only a walk that called the fill can paint.
DW-5 and DW-6 (forms step 2 R2, 2026-11-08) read each side of an edge: words' top and bottom, ok's left, bottom and top.
A child drawn upside down lands 5 points off at the vertical edges (words at 35..170, ok at 0..35), so (5,31), (5,166)
and ok's rows go wrong under a flip. The walk itself also calls makeDisplay; the fixture's own call before it stays, as step 1 built it.
